Description: build against Debian's packaged Go module sources
 Debian ships the modules under /usr/share/gocode/src instead of a module
 cache.  Point go.mod at those directories so the build stays offline without
 vendoring, while keeping the go directive (and with it net/http's Go 1.22+
 ServeMux behavior; GOPATH mode falls back to the old mux and breaks the
 local API routes).
Author: Kevin Watt <k@funmula.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-27

--- a/go.mod	2026-10-27 09:15:49.096275784 +0800
+++ b/go.mod	2026-10-27 09:15:49.098275815 +0800
@@ -9,3 +9,11 @@
 )
 
 require github.com/clipperhouse/uax29/v2 v2.7.0
+
+replace github.com/Microsoft/go-winio => /usr/share/gocode/src/github.com/Microsoft/go-winio
+
+replace github.com/godbus/dbus/v5 => /usr/share/gocode/src/github.com/godbus/dbus
+
+replace github.com/clipperhouse/uax29/v2 => /usr/share/gocode/src/github.com/clipperhouse/uax29/v2
+
+replace golang.org/x/sys => /usr/share/gocode/src/golang.org/x/sys
